  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Washington received $443M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Washington had 2,623 awards with an average award size of $169K, and obligations fell 97.7% year over year. Past fiscal years show larger totals: FY22 was $12.1B, FY23 was $13B, FY24 was $15.4B, FY25 was $15.9B, and FY26 was $19.5B. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $339M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $56.8M and the Department of Agriculture with $11M. Battelle Memorial Institute is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $140M, followed by Hanford Tank Waste Operations & Closure, LLC with $117M and Bechtel National, Inc. with $73M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry by obligations with $140M, followed by Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal with $117M and an entry labeled Unknown at $73M. Note that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
