        "body": "Obligations in Washington are $443M for FY2027 to date, and obligations fell 97.7% year over year. Award activity in Washington shows 2,623 awards with an average award size of $169K. FY2026 obligations were $19.5B and FY2027 to date is markedly lower in absolute terms. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is federal spending concentrated in Washington?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in Washington with $339M in obligations for FY2027 to date. Battelle Memorial Institute is the largest vendor with $140M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry with $140M. Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal is the next largest industry with $117M, supported by Hanford Tank Waste Operations & Closure, LLC receiving $117M."
      }
